[center][size=6][b]Spleak[/b][/size]
[size=4]Local split-screen for PEAK[/size]

[i]Two climbers. One PC. One window.[/i][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]What is it?[/b][/size]
Spleak turns PEAK into a couch co-op game. Player 1 climbs on keyboard and mouse or a second gamepad, player 2 grabs a gamepad, and the screen splits down the middle. You both share one mountain, one run and one fate.

There is no second copy of the game to launch, no second Steam account and no Nucleus Co-op setup. The game runs once and draws two views, so it is lighter on your PC too.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]A real menu option[/b] - a new [i]Play Split-Screen[/i] sign on the title menu, right under Play Offline. Pick Play Offline any time for a normal solo game.
[*][b]Two of everything[/b] - each player has their own camera, stamina bar, inventory, prompts and name tags.
[*][b]Two gamepads (new in 0.2.0)[/b] - connect a second gamepad and player 1 can play on it too. Player 1 switches between keyboard/mouse and their gamepad just by using either.
[*][b]Full controls for player 2[/b] - the game's normal gamepad layout, including the emote wheel and backpack wheel.
[*][b]Player 2's own passport[/b] - customise their scout with the gamepad. Their look is saved and comes back next time.
[*][b]Sound for both[/b] - every sound plays for whichever player is closer, panned to the side it is on. One shared soundtrack.
[*][b]Weather per player[/b] - fog, wind, snow storms, the storm sky and lava haze show on the half of the player who is in them.
[*][b]Injuries, passing out and death[/b] apply to the right player. A player who is down spectates the other one until revived.
[*][b]Side by side or top and bottom[/b] - one setting.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]PEAK on Steam
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases]BepInEx 5[/url] (x64). Mod managers install it for you.
[*]A gamepad for player 2 (Xbox, PlayStation through Steam Input, or any controller the game supports), and optionally a second one for player 1
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[b]With Vortex or another mod manager:[/b] install as usual.

[b]By hand:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx 5 into the PEAK folder and start the game once.
[*]Open the downloaded zip and copy the [b]BepInEx[/b] folder into the PEAK folder (Steam: right-click PEAK > Manage > Browse local files). Say yes to merging folders.
[/list]

[size=5][b]How to play[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Plug in a gamepad before starting PEAK.
[*]On the title menu, pick [b]Play Split-Screen[/b].
[*]Player 2 appears next to player 1 and the screen splits.
[/list]
In the airport, player 2 gets their own passport after a few seconds: hold it and use it like any item. D-pad or stick to move, A to pick, LB/RB for tabs, B to close.

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
[b]BepInEx\config\orchen17.peak.splitscreen.cfg[/b] appears after the first launch:
[list]
[*][b]SideBySide[/b] - true for left/right, false for top/bottom.
[*][b]Player2Hud[/b] - player 2's own HUD.
[*][b]Player2Sound[/b] - sound for both players, or only from player 1's position.
[*][b]TwoGamepads[/b] - let player 1 play on a second gamepad (on by default).
[*][b]Enabled[/b] - turn the mod off without uninstalling.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Split screen works in offline games only. Online lobbies are left untouched.
[*]Two players only.
[*]Player 2's passport offers what your account has unlocked.
[*]Music and background ambience follow player 1.
[*]This is a first release. The early mountain has had the most testing; later biomes and the ending have had less. Bug reports are very welcome.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Bugs[/b][/size]
Please report problems in the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/preplexo/peak-splitscreen/issues]GitHub[/url] and attach [b]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/b] from the run where it went wrong.

[i]Spleak is an unofficial fan mod. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the makers of PEAK.[/i]
